-## Optional jobs from KenshiQOL (private test)
-
-Thanks to **Steel**, author of [KenshiQOL](https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3772744830).
-**Original source:** the `src` folder distributed with the original mod; see `ORIGIN_Steel_jobs.md` in the test package for attribution and integration details. No separate source repository is verified.
-
-All three switches are under **MCM → KEO → Backpacks and jobs**, independently OFF by default. They change during play. Disabling one keeps its queued job rows and pauses its execution; it does not clear other orders. Do not enable the original KenshiQOL alongside these features.
-
-- **Gather Output:** right-click a machine with an output inventory and choose **Gather output**. SHIFT adds it to the ordinary Jobs queue. Uses native collection and movement.
-- **Stock Counter:** right-click your own shop counter and choose **Stock shop counter**. SHIFT makes it a recurring job. Deposits carried products from assigned Gather Output machines; without such machine jobs, uses native resource classification. This is stocking, not selling: no money changes hands. Filled or incompatible counters are skipped. Unequipped ordinary inventory grids are supported; foreign ownership and custom inventory callbacks are conservatively refused.
-- **Cyclic waypoints:** with its switch ON, SHIFT + right-click on open ground appends a waypoint for the characters selected at that click. The ordinary Jobs panel supports reordering and removal. Rows show coordinates; native saves retain the route. Existing ordinary movement orders are unaffected when this feature is OFF. Up to64 points per character are accepted.
-
-Use a separate test save for the first collection → counter delivery → save/load check. Offline checks passed; this is not yet an in-game acceptance claim.
